A-NAS serves the companion under /companion, not under the Harness route /dsh-pet-7340, and
its desktop is only served at /, so only the route segment changes. The animations then come
from dsh-pet's own address, /companion/thumb/<asset root>/<name>.<ext> (the asset root is the
configuration key, main), with the installed animation pool appended as ?v= when the page
knows it (RuntimePet.assetVersion), so the files can be cached for good and a pool switch is
never answered from the cache. This replaces 0001, which served /companion/animations/<name>.

